profile.comment=Quality presets. Low and Medium target 60 FPS on mid-range GPUs at 1080p; High targets 60 FPS on stronger GPUs; Ultra and Cinematic favour quality (Cinematic is meant for screenshots). These are goals, not measured guarantees.


option.COLOR_PROFILE=Colour Profile
option.COLOR_PROFILE.comment=Natural: neutral, no grading. Vibrant: richer greens and skies with controlled contrast (default). Cinematic: filmic contrast with subtle colour separation. Realistic: photographic, restrained. Fantasy: expressive colours. Custom: uses the sliders under Post Processing.
value.COLOR_PROFILE.0=Natural
value.COLOR_PROFILE.1=Vibrant
value.COLOR_PROFILE.2=Cinematic
value.COLOR_PROFILE.3=Realistic
value.COLOR_PROFILE.4=Fantasy
value.COLOR_PROFILE.5=Custom
option.TONEMAP=Tone Mapping
option.TONEMAP.comment=How bright light is compressed to the screen. Meridian Filmic keeps the hue of bright coloured light. Khronos Neutral keeps colours closest to their textures. Reinhard is simple and soft.
value.TONEMAP.0=Meridian Filmic
value.TONEMAP.1=Khronos PBR Neutral
value.TONEMAP.2=Reinhard
option.EXPOSURE_BIAS=Exposure
option.EXPOSURE_BIAS.comment=Brightens or darkens the whole image, in camera stops.
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE=Automatic Exposure
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE.comment=Adapts to the scene like your eyes do (darker caves look brighter after a moment). When off, exposure only follows the time of day.
option.ADAPTATION_SPEED=Adaptation Speed
option.ADAPTATION_SPEED.comment=How fast automatic exposure reacts.
option.NIGHT_BRIGHTNESS=Night Brightness
option.NIGHT_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How bright moonlit and starlit nights are. Real nights are far darker than a screen can show; this lifts them for play.

option.SUN_BRIGHTNESS=Sunlight
option.MOON_BRIGHTNESS=Moonlight
option.SKY_LIGHT_STRENGTH=Sky Light
option.SKY_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Ambient light from the sky in shaded areas.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH=Block Light
option.BLOCKLIGHT_TEMPERATURE=Block Light Colour
option.BLOCKLIGHT_TEMPERATURE.comment=Colour temperature (K) for light sources without a specific colour.
suffix.BLOCKLIGHT_TEMPERATURE= K
option.CAVE_MIN_LIGHT=Cave Minimum Light
option.CAVE_MIN_LIGHT.comment=A small amount of light everywhere so unlit caves are not pure black.
option.HAND_LIGHT=Held Light
option.HAND_LIGHT.comment=Torches and other light sources in your hands light up nearby surfaces, in their own colour.
option.SUBSURFACE_SCATTERING=Subsurface Scattering
option.SUBSURFACE_SCATTERING.comment=Light shines through leaves, grass and snow.
option.AMBIENT_OCCLUSION=Ambient Occlusion
option.AMBIENT_OCCLUSION.comment=Soft darkening in corners and crevices.
option.AO_STRENGTH=Ambient Occlusion Strength

option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Size of the shadow map (split into four cascades). Higher is sharper and more expensive.
option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far shadows reach, in blocks.
option.SHADOW_FILTER=Shadow Softness Model
option.SHADOW_FILTER.comment=Hard: crisp edges. Soft: uniformly soft edges. Physical: sharp near the caster, softer further away, like real sunlight.
value.SHADOW_FILTER.0=Hard
value.SHADOW_FILTER.1=Soft
value.SHADOW_FILTER.2=Physical
option.SHADOW_SAMPLES=Shadow Samples
option.SHADOW_SAMPLES.comment=Samples per pixel for soft shadows. More is smoother.
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Shadow Softness
option.CONTACT_SHADOWS=Contact Shadows
option.CONTACT_SHADOWS.comment=Fine shadows where objects touch surfaces.
option.COLORED_SHADOWS=Coloured Shadows
option.COLORED_SHADOWS.comment=Stained glass and other translucent blocks cast coloured shadows.
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS=Cloud Shadows

option.PBR_MODE=Material Source
option.PBR_MODE.comment=LabPBR reads normal and specular maps from your resource pack (LabPBR 1.3). Built-in uses the pack's own material values for vanilla textures.
value.PBR_MODE.0=Built-in
value.PBR_MODE.1=LabPBR
option.HARDCODED_MATERIALS=Built-in Materials
option.HARDCODED_MATERIALS.comment=Metals, glass, ice and other blocks get realistic materials when the resource pack has no specular map.
option.NORMAL_MAPPING=Normal Maps
option.NORMAL_MAP_STRENGTH=Normal Map Strength
option.NORMAL_MAP_Y_FLIP=Flip Normal Map Green
option.NORMAL_MAP_Y_FLIP.comment=Turn on only if bumps look inverted with your resource pack.
option.PARALLAX_OCCLUSION=Parallax Depth
option.PARALLAX_OCCLUSION.comment=Uses the resource pack's height maps to give surfaces real depth.
option.POM_DEPTH=Parallax Depth Amount
option.POM_SAMPLES=Parallax Quality
option.POM_SELF_SHADOW=Parallax Self-Shadowing
option.EMISSIVE_ORES=Emissive Ores
option.EMISSIVE_ORES.comment=Makes the mineral specks of ores glow faintly (built-in materials only; resource-pack emission is used as is). 0 = off, as in reality.
option.EMISSION_STRENGTH=Emission Strength
option.EMISSION_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of glowing parts of textures.

option.SSR=Screen-Space Reflections
option.SSR.comment=Reflects what is visible on screen. Anything off screen falls back to the sky (never black).
option.SSR_STEPS=Reflection Quality
option.SSR_MAX_ROUGHNESS=Reflection Roughness Limit
option.SSR_MAX_ROUGHNESS.comment=Rougher surfaces than this use sky reflections only (cheaper).
option.SKY_REFLECTIONS=Sky Reflections

option.COLORED_LIGHTING=Coloured Light
option.COLORED_LIGHTING.comment=Torches, lava, soul fire, sea lanterns and other lights colour the surfaces around them. Light never passes through walls: brightness follows vanilla light, colour comes from a voxel light volume around you.
option.CL_VOLUME=Coloured Light Range
value.CL_VOLUME.0=Near (128 x 64 x 128)
value.CL_VOLUME.1=Medium (192 x 96 x 192)
value.CL_VOLUME.2=Far (256 x 128 x 256)
option.CL_ITERATIONS=Coloured Light Speed
option.CL_ITERATIONS.comment=How quickly coloured light settles after changes.
option.CL_BRIGHTNESS=Coloured Light Strength
option.INDIRECT_SUN=Bounced Sunlight
option.INDIRECT_SUN.comment=Sunlight reflected from nearby sunlit surfaces into shade (reflective shadow maps).
option.RSM_SAMPLES=Bounced Light Quality
option.INDIRECT_SUN_STRENGTH=Bounced Light Strength

option.WATER_WAVES=Waves
option.WATER_WAVES.comment=Wind-driven waves: ocean swells, lake ripples and flowing-water chop.
option.WAVE_HEIGHT=Wave Height
option.WAVE_SPEED=Wave Speed
option.WATER_REFRACTION=Refraction
option.WATER_CLARITY=Water Clarity
option.WATER_CAUSTICS=Caustics
option.WATER_VANILLA_TEXTURE=Vanilla Water Texture
option.WATER_VANILLA_TEXTURE.comment=Keep the resource pack's water pattern on the surface.

option.WATER_SIM=Interactive Water
option.WATER_SIM.comment=You, while walking, swimming or jumping into water, and your boat create real waves that spread, reflect off shores and fade.
option.WATER_SIM_RES=Simulation Quality
option.WATER_SIM_RES.comment=Width of the simulated area around you. Larger areas let waves travel further before they fade out.
value.WATER_SIM_RES.0=Low (32 blocks)
value.WATER_SIM_RES.1=Medium (64 blocks)
value.WATER_SIM_RES.2=High (128 blocks)
value.WATER_SIM_RES.3=Ultra (256 blocks)
option.WATER_SIM_STRENGTH=Ripple Strength
option.WATER_SIM_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of every disturbance: walking, swimming, splashes and boats.
option.WATER_SIM_SPEED=Wave Propagation
option.WATER_SIM_SPEED.comment=How fast ripples spread across the water.
suffix.WATER_SIM_SPEED= blocks/s
option.WATER_SIM_DAMPING=Ripple Damping
option.WATER_SIM_DAMPING.comment=How quickly ripples lose energy. Short ripples always fade faster than long waves.
value.WATER_SIM_DAMPING.0=Low
value.WATER_SIM_DAMPING.1=Normal
value.WATER_SIM_DAMPING.2=High
option.WATER_BOAT_WAKE=Boat Wake Strength
option.WATER_SPLASH_STRENGTH=Player Splash Strength
option.WATER_SPLASH_STRENGTH.comment=Size of the splash when you jump or fall into water.

option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUDS=Volumetric Clouds
option.CLOUD_QUALITY=Cloud Quality
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.0=Low
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.1=Medium
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.2=High
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.3=Ultra
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.4=Cinematic
option.CLOUD_QUALITY.comment=Low: simple shapes and lighting. Medium: full cloud shapes. High: detailed lighting. Ultra and Cinematic: longer marches, finer scattering.
option.CLOUD_RES=Cloud Resolution
option.CLOUD_RES.comment=Clouds are rendered at reduced resolution and rebuilt over several frames.
value.CLOUD_RES.1=Full
value.CLOUD_RES.2=Half
value.CLOUD_RES.4=Quarter
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE=Cloud Coverage
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE.comment=Average share of the sky covered. Weather systems make some regions clear and others overcast.
option.CLOUD_DENSITY=Cloud Density
option.CLOUD_DENSITY.comment=Thickness of the cloud material: higher values give darker, more solid clouds.
option.WEATHER_CLOUDS=Weather-Based Clouds
option.WEATHER_CLOUDS.comment=Large weather systems drift over: open blue sky in some regions, cloud banks and overcast in others. Off: the same coverage everywhere.
option.CUMULONIMBUS=Storm Clouds
option.CUMULONIMBUS.comment=Towering cumulonimbus up to 9 km in thunderstorms.
option.CLOUD_ALTITUDE=Cloud Altitude
suffix.CLOUD_ALTITUDE= m
option.CLOUD_SPEED=Wind Speed
option.CLOUD_SPEED.comment=How fast clouds drift. Storms always blow faster than calm weather.
option.CIRRUS_CLOUDS=Cirrus Clouds
option.CIRRUS_AMOUNT=Cirrus Amount

option.HAZE_DENSITY=Haze
option.HAZE_DENSITY.comment=Amount of haze and mist in the air (also rises with rain).
option.AERIAL_PERSPECTIVE=Distance Fog
option.AERIAL_PERSPECTIVE.comment=How strongly distant terrain fades into the atmosphere.
option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHT=Light Shafts
option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHT.comment=Visible sun and moon rays through haze, trees and windows; light shafts under water.
option.VL_STEPS=Light Shaft Quality
option.VL_STRENGTH=Light Shaft Strength
option.BORDER_FOG=Edge Fog
option.BORDER_FOG.comment=Fades the edge of the loaded world into the sky.

option.WET_SURFACES=Wet Surfaces
option.WET_SURFACES.comment=Rain darkens porous blocks and makes smooth ones glossy; they dry slowly afterwards.
option.LIGHTNING_FLASH=Lightning Flashes
option.SNOW_OVERLAY=Snow Cover
option.SNOW_OVERLAY.comment=Snow settles on the tops of exposed blocks, leaves and plants in snowy biomes, more while it snows. Walls stay clear.
option.SNOW_AMOUNT=Snow Cover Amount
option.AURORA=Aurora
value.AURORA.0=Off
value.AURORA.1=Some Nights
value.AURORA.2=Every Night
option.AURORA.comment=Green and red auroral curtains high in the night sky. Some Nights: roughly one night in four.
option.AURORA_BRIGHTNESS=Aurora Brightness
option.RAINBOWS=Rainbows
option.RAINBOWS.comment=Primary and secondary rainbow opposite the sun after rain, while the air is still wet and the sun is below 42 degrees.
option.RAINBOW_STRENGTH=Rainbow Strength
option.RAIN_STREAKS=Realistic Rain
option.RAIN_STREAKS.comment=Rain drops reflect the sky and lights instead of looking like grey lines.
option.RAIN_OPACITY=Rain Visibility
option.RAIN_WIND_LEAN=Rain Wind Slant
option.RAIN_RIPPLES=Rain Ripples
option.PUDDLES=Puddles
option.PUDDLE_AMOUNT=Puddle Amount
option.PUDDLE_AMOUNT.comment=Share of open, level ground that collects water in heavy rain: about 8 % at 1.0, 3 % at 0.5, 20 % at 2.0.
option.PUDDLE_SIZE=Puddle Size
option.PUDDLE_SIZE.comment=Typical size of individual puddles (1.0: a few blocks across).

option.MOON_TEXTURE=Moon Detail
option.MOON_TEXTURE.comment=NASA LRO lunar colour and LOLA elevation maps. 8K uses more video memory.
value.MOON_TEXTURE.0=2K
value.MOON_TEXTURE.1=4K
value.MOON_TEXTURE.2=8K
option.MOON_SIZE=Moon Size
option.MOON_SIZE.comment=1.0 is the Moon's real apparent size.
option.SUN_SIZE=Sun Size
option.STARS=Stars
option.STARS.comment=Real star positions, brightness and colours from NASA's Deep Star Maps.
option.STAR_BRIGHTNESS=Star Brightness
option.MILKY_WAY=Milky Way
option.MILKY_WAY_BRIGHTNESS=Milky Way Brightness
option.ECLIPSES=Eclipses
option.ECLIPSES.comment=The Moon follows an inclined orbit, so solar and lunar eclipses happen occasionally.
option.EARTHSHINE=Earthshine
option.EARTHSHINE.comment=The dark part of a crescent Moon glows faintly with light reflected from the Earth.

option.END_SPACE=Deep Space Sky
option.END_SPACE.comment=Replaces the End sky with a galaxy backdrop (NASA data) and space objects.
option.END_NEBULAE=Nebulae
option.END_LIGHT_STRENGTH=Accretion Disk Light
option.END_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly the black hole's disk lights the End islands.
option.BLACK_HOLE=Black Hole
option.BLACK_HOLE.comment=A ray-traced black hole with gravitational lensing and a glowing accretion disk.
option.BH_SIZE=Black Hole Size
option.BH_DISK_BRIGHTNESS=Disk Brightness
option.BH_LENSING_STEPS=Lensing Quality
option.END_PLANETS=Planets
option.END_PLANETS.comment=Procedural planets slowly orbiting in the End sky (artistic, not real objects).

option.NETHER_FOG_DENSITY=Smoke Density
option.NETHER_SMOKE=Moving Smoke
option.HEAT_DISTORTION=Heat Shimmer
option.HEAT_STRENGTH=Heat Shimmer Strength
option.NETHER_ASH=Ash

option.PURKINJE=Night Vision Colour
option.PURKINJE.comment=In the dark, colours fade and shift blue, as human vision does.
option.BLOOM=Bloom
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH=Bloom Strength
option.VIGNETTE=Vignette
option.CUSTOM_SATURATION=Custom: Saturation
option.CUSTOM_VIBRANCE=Custom: Vibrance
option.CUSTOM_CONTRAST=Custom: Contrast
option.CUSTOM_WHITE_BALANCE=Custom: White Balance
suffix.CUSTOM_WHITE_BALANCE= K
option.CUSTOM_SHADOW_TINT=Custom: Split Toning

option.DH_CHUNK_FADE=DH Chunk Fade
option.DH_CHUNK_FADE.comment=With Distant Horizons: vanilla chunks dissolve into the LOD terrain over the last part of the render distance instead of ending at a hard line.
option.LOD_FADE=Distant Terrain Edge Fade
option.LOD_FADE.comment=How strongly the very edge of Distant Horizons or Voxy terrain fades into the sky.

option.TAA=Temporal Anti-Aliasing
option.TAA.comment=Smooths edges and the noise of soft shadows, reflections and clouds over several frames.
option.TAA_SHARPNESS=Sharpening

option.STATIC_NOISE=Static Noise (diagnostic)
option.STATIC_NOISE.comment=Freezes all per-frame sampling noise. If a light or shadow flicker stops with this on, it comes from stochastic sampling; otherwise it has another cause. Leave off for normal play.
